          "We ran the paper's 8 R scripts in the order they depend on each other, each in a separate R or Python session, for at most 1 minute per script. We did not install packages the scripts need.\n\n**6 of 8 scripts ran to the end**: 2 did not reproduce.\n\n| Script | Result | What happened |\n|---|---|---|\n| def&#95;a.R | Ran to the end |  |\n| def&#95;b.R | Ran to the end |  |\n| fn&#95;user.R | Stopped with an error | <code>Error in nonexistent&#95;fun&#95;xyz(1) : could not find function \"nonexistent&#95;fun&#95;xyz\"<\/code> |\n| msg&#95;only.R | Ran to the end |  |\n| quiet.R | Ran to the end |  |\n| setwd&#95;var.R | Ran to the end |  |\n| user.R | Stopped with an error | <code>Error in eval(e, envir = env) : object 'shared&#95;x' not found<\/code> |\n| warn.R | Ran to the end |  |\n\n### How to make your code run on another computer\n\nWe ran your code on a clean computer, the way a reader or reviewer would. Below is each problem we found, the scripts it affects, and how to fix it. Fix them in the order given: a problem near the top can cause the ones below it.\n\n**A script uses something it does not create or load itself.**\n\n- <code>fn&#95;user.R<\/code>\n- <code>user.R<\/code>\n\nUsually the object was still in your R session from earlier work, or another script made it.\n\n1. Restart R (in RStudio: Session > Restart R).\n2. Run each script from top to bottom, and fix what is missing.\n3. If a script needs results of another, save them to a file in the first script and read them in the second.\n4. Load every package with <code>library()<\/code> at the top.\n\n### Other problems in the files\n\n- setwd&#95;var.R calls setwd(), which sets the folder the script runs in. We replaced the call with one that does nothing, so the script ran from the top folder of the project. A folder on your own computer does not exist on another; paths written from the project's top folder work everywhere.\n\n### Comparison with the paper\n\nWe found no statistical tests in the paper to compare with the output of the code."
